# Every text file is LF in the working tree, on every OS. Without this, a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true (git's Windows default, and GitHub's windows runners') wrote CRLF, and eight tests
# that read source as text failed on `\r` — every Windows CI run since 2026-09-23 (run 37552051536).
# The repository content was always LF; this makes the working tree match it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored third-party code is kept byte for byte as published: its hashes are pinned (third_party/*/VENDORED.md).
third_party/** -text
